Z||000000||bHooper||05-10-2000||06:58 AM||||First off, I thought I put a post up last night about the following... but I dont see it... hmm.  Secondly... THE CAR CRANKS... THE CAR CRANKS!!!<P>Now to serious business.  I have the following technical problems that I need to work out on my GT.<P>1) I need some advice on properly aligning the cradle.  What is the "easist way"?  So far I have one cradle bolt in (LF) and the left strut in place.  I need to figure this one out.<P>2) I have stripped the manifold where the fuel line return is (under the plenum, but closest to the battery).  Can I have this retapped?  Is it better to replace it?  If so, how much trouble is that to dissmantle?  What kind of bit do I need to remove the plenum?<P>3)The clutch, when depressed, has no feel in it whatsoever!  Do I not have something properly aligned?  Or is it a bad slave cylinder?  And yes, I no that I need to change my pedal, but not today.<P>Any advice is welcome!  At this moment I am so happy that my baby is running, after setting for 4 years!  I know that I have a lot of work to do... a lot to do in the next couple of days.<P>Thanks,<BR>hoop<p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 05-10-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||05-10-2000||07:41 AM||||Ok, I've had a little time to look at the haynes book, and the part that is stripped out is the "fuel block".  This is where the fuel ines come into the injection system.<P>How hard is it to swap out?  What kind of bit do I need to remove the plenum?  <P>There is a '85 GT at the salvage yard, will it's fuel block work on my car?  <P>Thanks,<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-10-2000||10:34 AM||||most V6 parts from all years are interchangeable. I imagine is should fit.<P>The cradle is self aligning as long as the bushings are good. There is no provision to adjust that. If you changed the cradle bushings then you should have the wheel alignment checked. A wheel alignment done to the old, worn, bushings may not be entirely correct on the new ones. It will likely be OK unless the old bushings where really rotten, but it should be checked.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||05-10-2000||11:16 AM||||To remove the star shaped chrome bolts on the plenum just use a 12pt socket or wrench. As for the clutch there is a huge thread called "clutch info uncovered" use the search funtion and read your little heart out||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||05-10-2000||02:24 PM||||I will take this into consideration.  Although, I am still not sure of the best way to line up the cradle to the mounting points.<P>Also, I found a mysterious hose that comes from the back (corner side) of the air cleaner, follows the firewall and then seems to be "cut" and leeds to nowhere.  Just a open hose.  What is this?  Where does it go?  Is it fine as is?<P>Thanks,<BR>hoop||||reg||1
