Z||000006||bHooper||05-10-2000||03:45 PM||||Ok, Bob from Kick Hill is sending me a fuel block and flare nut, so that I can replace the one I have.<P>Still reading the "clutch info uncovered thread"<P>Reading that is kinda like the episode of Star Trek, where McCoy had to have the spiked hair dryer put on his head to gain the knowledge to repair Spock's Brain!  <P>I am feeling smarter smarter smarter... damn it Jim!  <P>I have learned, that I need to do the following things to "repair and inspect" the clutch hydraulic system:<BR>1) drain system<BR>2) inspet and clean slave and master cylinder<BR>3) rebuild or replace slave cylinder<BR>4) check clutch pedal<BR>and 5) refill master cylinder with ATF<P>Also, I havent checked to see if the "repair shop" that dismantled the tranny 4 years ago, disconected something at the master cylinder!<P>So now, aside from time and money, I only have one real problem left... How to reinstall the cradle to the car properly....<P>Thanks,<BR>hoop||||reg||1
