Z||000026||bHooper||05-15-2000||02:00 PM||||well, i purchased a rebuild kit from NAPA on saturday.  after some investigation, i discovered the following:<P>1) the nut on the line from the master cylinder is frozen to the salve.<BR>2) the colar that the boot goes around is also frozen to the slave, so i cant remove it to rebuild the slave<P>so, after looking at the piece's of junk that Advance Auto and Auto Zone have for sell, and getting quotes from Pep Boys, NAPA, and Carquest... i have ordered the <B>original GM part</B> for $114.<P>I believe that that is my best bet.  Bendix is not available in my area; the most common brands are Raybestos, Truetorque, and United.<P>So, tommorow evening, i will free the hydraulic line, completly drain the system, and start to work on the body.  my new slave will be in on wednesday!<P>hoop||||reg||1
